Feature: SAM3 Prompt Enhancement — Gemini-Generated Segmentation Descriptions
  As a platform operator
  I want Gemini to generate detailed visual descriptions for each detected surface
  So that SAM3 can accurately segment and track the surface across video frames

  Background:
    Given the BIT platform uses Gemini for surface detection
    And SAM3 (fal.ai) for per-frame surface tracking
    And currently SAM3 receives only a single center-point with no text guidance
    And this causes SAM3 to fail tracking, producing all-black output

  # ── Gemini Prompt Generation ──

  Scenario: Gemini generates SAM3 prompt alongside surface detection
    Given a video frame with a visible surface
    When Gemini detects a surface of type "plaster wall surface"
    Then the response includes a "sam3_prompt" field
    And the prompt contains a visual description of the surface
    And the prompt describes color, texture, shape, and edges
    And the prompt does NOT contain viability or brand-safety commentary

  Scenario: Gemini generates SAM3 prompt for multiple surfaces
    Given a video frame with 5 visible surfaces
    When Gemini detects all 5 surfaces
    Then each surface in the response has a unique "sam3_prompt"
    And each prompt describes that specific surface's visual appearance

  Scenario: Non-Gemini detection engines gracefully handle missing prompt
    Given the detection engine is "yolo" or "basic"
    When surfaces are detected without SAM3 prompts
    Then SurfaceItem.Sam3Prompt is null
    And the SAM3 payload excludes the "prompt" field
    And no errors are thrown

  # ── SAM3 Payload Enhancement ──

  Scenario: SAM3 receives full boundary as point prompts with object grouping
    Given a surface with boundary [[790,250],[1080,250],[1080,520],[790,520]]
    And a valid SAM3 prompt from Gemini
    When SAM3 tracking is invoked
    Then the payload includes "point_prompts" with all 4 corner points plus center
    And each point has frame_index, x, y, label=1, and object_id=0
    And the payload includes "box_prompts" with the full bounding box
    And the box has frame_index and object_id=0
    And the payload includes "prompt" with the Gemini-generated description
    And "apply_mask" is set to true
    And "detection_threshold" is set to 0.3
    And "video_output_type" is "X264 (.mp4)"

  Scenario: SAM3 tracking succeeds with enhanced prompt
    Given a surface with valid boundary and SAM3 prompt
    When SAM3 processes the video
    Then the returned segmented video is not all-black
    And the video file size is greater than 100KB
    And the event log shows TRACKING_COMPLETE with success

  # ── Render Compositing with Luma Mask ──

  Scenario: Render uses SAM3 video as per-pixel luma mask
    Given a completed SAM3 tracking job returning a segmented video
    When the render pipeline composites the asset
    Then ffmpeg extracts luma from the SAM3 video as a binary mask
    And the asset is scaled to video dimensions and converted to RGBA
    And the SAM3 mask is applied as alpha channel via alphamerge
    And the masked asset is overlaid on the ORIGINAL source video
    And the output format is yuv420p with H.264 encoding

  Scenario: Render output shows asset only on tracked surface
    Given a completed render job
    When the output video is opened
    Then the video shows the original scene content
    And the brand asset is visible ONLY on the tracked surface region
    And the background shows the original content without the asset
    And the asset visibility tracks the surface across frames

  # ── Data Integrity ──

  Scenario: SAM3 prompt survives detection-to-tracking round-trip
    Given Gemini detected surface "sf-01" with sam3_prompt "white plaster wall..."
    When the surface is persisted to the database
    And later retrieved for SAM3 tracking
    Then the prompt passed to SAM3 matches the Gemini-generated prompt
